# DOES NOT RUN. The server half of this profile fails during CUDA graph capture
# in DeepSeek-V4's fused kernels, which are built for the recipe's TP8/DP1 --
# see model_serving/profiles/ for the stack. Nothing is wrong with this file:
# the client half of a layout is layout-agnostic, and it is kept only so the
# pair stays together if the server side is ever revived.
#
# Client side of the tp2dp4 server profile. Parallelism is invisible over HTTP --
# same checkpoint, same chat template, same modes -- so this inherits everything
# and adds nothing. It exists because PROFILE names one file per side, and a
# sweep that asks for this layout has to find both.

PROFILE_BASE=deepseek_v4_tp8dp1_speculative
